11. Archives, Compression, and Backups

11.1 Create a Tar Archive

tar -cf backup.tar Documents/

Creates an uncompressed tar archive containing the Documents directory.

11.2 Create a Compressed Archive

tar -czf backup.tar.gz Documents/

The "-z" option uses gzip compression.

11.3 Extract an Archive

tar -tf backup.tar.gz
tar -xzf backup.tar.gz

- "-t" lists archive contents.
- "-x" extracts archive contents.
- "-f" specifies the archive file.
- "-z" handles gzip compression.

Inspect archive paths before extraction, especially when an archive comes from an untrusted source.

11.4 Verify File Integrity

sha256sum backup.tar.gz

Computes a SHA-256 digest for the archive.

A hash can help detect changes when compared with a trusted reference digest. A hash alone does not establish that the original file was authentic or safe.

