12. Package Management

On Debian-based systems, APT manages software packages and their dependencies.

12.1 Package Information

apt search wireshark
apt show wireshark
dpkg -l

- "apt search" searches package metadata.
- "apt show" displays package information.
- "dpkg -l" lists installed packages and their package states.

12.2 Install and Update

sudo apt update
sudo apt install package-name
sudo apt upgrade

"apt update" refreshes package metadata; it does not itself upgrade installed packages.

"apt install" installs a package and its required dependencies.

"apt upgrade" upgrades installed packages according to APT's normal upgrade rules.

Review proposed package changes before confirming, particularly on a penetration-testing workstation where tool versions and dependencies may be important.

12.3 Identify Package Ownership

dpkg -S /usr/bin/ssh

Searches installed package records for the package that owns the specified path.

Replace the example path with the file being investigated.

