13. Environment Variables and Shell Configuration

Environment variables influence how applications behave.

13.1 Inspect Variables

printenv
echo "$HOME"
echo "$PATH"

- "printenv" displays exported environment variables.
- "$HOME" identifies the user's home directory.
- "$PATH" lists directories searched for executable commands.

Avoid publishing complete environment dumps because they may contain sensitive information.

13.2 Temporary Variables

export LAB_MODE=testing
echo "$LAB_MODE"

Exports a variable to the current shell and child processes.

The value normally does not persist after the shell session ends unless it is configured in a shell startup file or another persistent configuration mechanism.

13.3 Command History

history

Displays commands recorded in the current shell's history.

Command history may contain sensitive arguments or operational details. Review it carefully before sharing terminal screenshots or diagnostic output.

