15. Advanced Troubleshooting Methodology

Effective troubleshooting begins with observation rather than arbitrary configuration changes.

Example: A Service Is Unavailable

Step 1 — Check service state

systemctl status SERVICE_NAME

Step 2 — Review recent logs

journalctl -u SERVICE_NAME -n 100

Step 3 — Check listening sockets

ss -lntp

Step 4 — Inspect network configuration

ip addr show
ip route

Step 5 — Test the relevant connection

Use a connection test appropriate to the service and authorized environment.

Step 6 — Record the findings

Document the observed failure, supporting output, corrective action, and verification result.

Replace "SERVICE_NAME" with the actual systemd unit name. These commands provide diagnostic evidence but do not independently identify every possible root cause.

