16. Common Command-Line Risks

Risk| Why it matters| Safer approach
Incorrect recursive path| Can modify or delete large directory trees| Verify paths before execution
Overwriting files with ">"| Existing output can be lost| Check the destination or use a new filename
Unnecessary root privileges| Increases the consequences of mistakes| Use least privilege
Killing the wrong PID| May interrupt essential services| Verify the process before termination
Extracting untrusted archives| May overwrite files or create unexpected paths| Inspect archive contents first
Sharing raw logs| May expose usernames, addresses, or secrets| Sanitize evidence
Changing network services remotely| Can disconnect the session| Plan access and recovery first

